{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_d9ad05f5bda622e1\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_d9ad05f5bda622e1/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Fictional placeholder contact details and QN handling\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_68b6c06c2198c6e02e87d841\", \"member_83bf399505a4fa8d03f5f1b6\", \"member_28bcdf8b10a3addf72c9e677\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether fake email addresses need QN and reports that two open versions of a note seem to differ.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks whether to use QN or proceed on SAFETY-8195, which uses someone@example.test in a made-up story, and reports that two open versions of a note seem to differ.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether fake email addresses need QN and how to handle SAFETY-2378.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the first QA tutor’s thread, the team lead asks to hold a final general-rule update until the current rule and change date are verified and to retain the surrounding fictional context with the flag; the thread does not answer the QA tutor’s task-handling question.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871321.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"For the tutor’s SAFETY-8195 task, the team lead answers that clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN and actual identifiable private data still needs separate review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"In the SAFETY-2378 thread, a tutor reports that the address uses an obvious placeholder domain rather than a real contact; this reply does not answer the QA tutor’s QN-handling question.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions say clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN after checking the surrounding material establishes that no real individual is identifiable. Actual identifiable private information, ambiguous details and separate QN triggers require review. The dated clarification replaces only the older help page’s blanket fictional-contact trigger.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ says verified fictional placeholders alone do not require QN if no real individual is identifiable and no separate trigger applies. It identifies the old help-page copy as not yet rewritten and directs reporting that stale copy for correction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The older help page’s Contact details section required initial quarantine even for made-up contact details; that section was superseded effective September 10, 2026, at 13:00 UTC and is not current handling.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 18 follow-up inspection records updated instructions, an updated FAQ and a posted announcement, but a help page still containing the blanket initial-quarantine wording. It records partial completion and no later repair within that record, not an unresolved general rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier documentation approval records the team lead’s approval of documentation and communication follow-up, with document updates still pending at approval; it does not establish that the work was completed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The project clarification records an effective date of September 10, 2026, at 13:00 UTC and replaces the blanket fictional-contact requirement only in the old help page’s Contact details section.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c13\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The batch announcement directs retaining the surrounding context and not extending the fictional-placeholder exception to unrelated controls. Verbatim quote: \\\"Retain the surrounding context.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors and a tutor ask whether fictional email details require QN; two report conflicting note versions.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance settles the general rule, but the old help-page wording remains stale; the team lead answered the tutor’s task, while the two QA tutors’ handling questions remain unresolved.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871321.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the first QA tutor’s thread, the team lead asked to retain the fictional context and hold a final general-rule update until the current rule and change date were verified.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871321.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"For SAFETY-8195, the team lead said clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN, while actual identifiable private data needs separate review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"For SAFETY-2378, a tutor describes an obvious placeholder domain, but the thread contains no answer to the QA tutor’s handling question.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current instructions require checking the surrounding material for identifiability and retaining ambiguous cases or separate QN triggers for review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The earlier documentation approval authorized follow-up work, and the September 18 inspection recorded updated instructions, an updated FAQ and a posted announcement, but a still-stale help page.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Update the documentation. Instruction: Correct the old help page’s Contact details section to match the current fictional-placeholder rule and preserve all separate review controls. Draft to copy: Please correct the QN help page’s Contact details section to reflect the clarification effective September 10, 2026:\\n- Clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN when the surrounding material establishes that no real individual is identifiable.\\n- Retain the surrounding context.\\n- Actual identifiable private information, uncertain fictional context or identifiability, and any separate QN trigger still require review.\\nReplace only the superseded blanket fictional-contact requirement; preserve unrelated safety controls and point readers to the current instructions and FAQ. Scope: Limit the correction to the superseded Contact details branch. Do not treat the documentation change as confirmation that either unresolved task meets the fictional-placeholder conditions. Changes (only these): correct Safety Classification — QN Help Page (v1.0), section 'Contact details'.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\", \"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c13\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"]}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The FAQ explicitly calls for correcting this stale copy, and the earlier inspection records that the correction remained unfinished. Repairing that specific conflict follows the settled rule rather than reopening general policy.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\", \"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871321.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): Two QA tutors and a tutor raise QN-handling questions, two report differing note versions, and the current FAQ identifies a stale help-page branch requiring correction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"If contact details could identify a real person, the fictional context is uncertain, or another required safety trigger applies, retain the task for review under the applicable rules.\\\". The project-wide fictional-contact clarification applies to this batch’s QN question and directs retaining cases outside the scoped exception for review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Retain the surrounding context.\\\". The announcement names this batch and the same fictional-contact issue, and directly instructs retaining context while preserving unrelated safety controls.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:8b4f76e9\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Update the instruction and FAQ wording and correct the old help-page copy.\\\". The project-wide documentation follow-up concerns the same clarification and directs correcting the old help-page copy; it does not certify completion.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:8b4f76e9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_68b6c06c2198c6e02e87d841\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_68b6c06c2198c6e02e87d841 is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor asks for handling; a QA tutor asks to establish that no real individual is identifiable, and the team lead requests verification of the current rule and change date. No message answers the task-handling question.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871263.000058\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871321.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790871365.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_83bf399505a4fa8d03f5f1b6\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_83bf399505a4fa8d03f5f1b6 is RESOLVED_IN_THREAD: The team lead directly answers the tutor’s SAFETY-8195 question: clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN for this task, with actual identifiable private data subject to separate review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908195.000063\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908249.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908292.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790908330.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_28bcdf8b10a3addf72c9e677\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_28bcdf8b10a3addf72c9e677 is UNRESOLVED: A tutor describes the domain as an obvious placeholder, but does not answer the QA tutor’s handling question or provide an authoritative instruction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922378.000060\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790922435.000113\"]}, {\"stateme